1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:02,467
The microwave beeps.

2
00:00:02,467 --> 00:00:04,567
It's done — but
your food isn't.

3
00:00:04,567 --> 00:00:05,633
In thick food,

4
00:00:05,633 --> 00:00:08,200
the waves mostly heat
the outer layers.

5
00:00:08,200 --> 00:00:09,233
When they stop,

6
00:00:09,233 --> 00:00:10,667
the outside is hot —

7
00:00:10,667 --> 00:00:12,667
the middle is still
catching up.

8
00:00:12,667 --> 00:00:14,633
That heat keeps
flowing inward,

9
00:00:14,633 --> 00:00:16,867
from the hot outside
to the cooler center —

10
00:00:16,867 --> 00:00:18,767
no microwaves needed.

11
00:00:18,767 --> 00:00:20,300
That's standing time.

12
00:00:20,300 --> 00:00:22,733
Food keeps cooking
after the oven stops —

13
00:00:22,733 --> 00:00:25,533
its temperature can climb
several more degrees.

14
00:00:25,867 --> 00:00:27,467
It's not extra heating.

15
00:00:27,467 --> 00:00:28,833
It's the same heat,

16
00:00:28,833 --> 00:00:29,700
spreading out.

17
00:00:30,067 --> 00:00:31,733
Food-safety guides
say let it stand

18
00:00:31,733 --> 00:00:33,333
at least three minutes —

19
00:00:33,333 --> 00:00:35,367
then check it
with a food thermometer.

20
00:00:35,667 --> 00:00:37,667
The beep means
the waves are done.

21
00:00:37,667 --> 00:00:40,333
Standing time lets
the heat finish the job.
